    <p>
      I direct Claude Code to build it. The operating layer is public, and it
      is <a href="https://github.com/sanlee-ys/agent-ops">agent-ops</a>. It
      holds the <code>PreToolUse</code> guards that enforce the security
      posture mechanically. It holds the working agreements that parallel
      sessions run under. It also holds an incident log at a deliberate
      severity bar, with the failures left in.
    </p>

    <h2 id="what-it-grew-into">The four repos</h2>
    <ul class="repo-grid">
      <li><strong><a href="https://github.com/sanlee-ys/notes-api">notes-api</a></strong><span>FastAPI REST service. The knowledge base and data layer.</span></li>
      <li><strong><a href="https://github.com/sanlee-ys/defense-news-classifier">defense-news-classifier</a></strong><span>LLM classifier with a real <Term id="eval">eval harness</Term>. Labels the content.</span></li>
      <li><strong><a href="https://github.com/sanlee-ys/kb-agent">kb-agent</a></strong><span><Term id="rag">RAG</Term> and tool-use agent. The hub that reasons over the system.</span></li>
      <li><strong><a href="https://github.com/sanlee-ys/learning-notes">learning-notes</a></strong><span>Plain-language notes on the techniques behind it all.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="ex-caption">All four repos are public. The ADRs and contract tests below live in those repos.</p>

